## R-transparency proof, checks 2-3: a semi-transparent front square over a
## larger, fully opaque back square. The light sits on the camera's own
## side of both planes, offset laterally so the segment from the back
## square's centre toward the light passes outside the front square's
## footprint -- the front casts no shadow on the back, so this fixture's
## golden stays valid whether the occluder reads only the nearest blocker
## or accumulates every one. Not third-party.
Display "transparency_composite.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [40]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.1]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [1.0] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [5 0 -5] "to" [0 0 0]
Sides 2
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.1] "Kd" [0.9]

AttributeBegin
	Color [0.2 0.3 0.9]
	Opacity [1 1 1]
	Polygon "P" [-1.2 -1.2 0  1.2 -1.2 0  1.2 1.2 0  -1.2 1.2 0]
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
	Translate 0 0 -2
	Color [0.8 0.2 0.2]
	Opacity [0.4 0.4 0.4]
	Polygon "P" [-0.4 -0.4 0  0.4 -0.4 0  0.4 0.4 0  -0.4 0.4 0]
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
